# Tests — MSA Schedule 4 claiming a Service Credit

Assertion-based tests for `Service_credit_claim`. The Measurement Period ends
on 31 January 2025 throughout, so the L-5.1 deadline is 2 March 2025, and the
window is tested on both sides of it: a claim on day 30 is in time, a claim on
day 31 is waived. Both branches of the L-5.2 settlement hierarchy are covered,
with their dates.

L-5.2's route is a pair of booleans rather than an enumeration, because Catala
1.2.1 cannot JSON-encode an enum-typed output and the scope was therefore
unexecutable through the interface the whole system answers questions with
(CE-0009). An assertion cannot catch that defect — assertions run under the
interpreter, which serialises nothing — so the guard against its return is
`scripts/check_executable.py`, run as step 6 of `scripts/check.sh`. What the
tests here add is the answer CE-0009 asked for, pinned on its own facts, plus
the invariant that the two route booleans are always opposites.

> Using ServiceCreditClaim

## L5_1_ClaimOnDayThirty

L-5.1: "within 30 days after the end of the Measurement Period" is inclusive
of the thirtieth day, so a claim on 2 March is in time.

```catala
#[test]
declaration scope TestL5_1_ClaimOnDayThirty:
  output r content ServiceCreditClaim.CreditClaim

scope TestL5_1_ClaimOnDayThirty:
  definition r equals
    output of ServiceCreditClaim.CreditClaim with {
      -- measurement_period_end: |2025-01-31|
      -- claim_made: true
      -- claim_date: |2025-03-02|
      -- claim_accepted_date: |2025-03-10|
      -- further_invoice_expected: true
      -- next_invoice_date: |2025-04-01|
    }
  assertion r.claim_deadline = |2025-03-02|
  assertion r.claim_in_time = true
  assertion r.waived = false
```

## L5_1_ClaimOnDayThirtyOne

L-5.1: one day later and the Service Credit is waived.

```catala
#[test]
declaration scope TestL5_1_ClaimOnDayThirtyOne:
  output r content ServiceCreditClaim.CreditClaim

scope TestL5_1_ClaimOnDayThirtyOne:
  definition r equals
    output of ServiceCreditClaim.CreditClaim with {
      -- measurement_period_end: |2025-01-31|
      -- claim_made: true
      -- claim_date: |2025-03-03|
      -- claim_accepted_date: |2025-03-10|
      -- further_invoice_expected: true
      -- next_invoice_date: |2025-04-01|
    }
  assertion r.claim_deadline = |2025-03-02|
  assertion r.claim_in_time = false
  assertion r.waived = true
```

## L5_1_EarlyClaim

L-5.1: a claim made promptly after the end of the period is plainly in time.

```catala
#[test]
declaration scope TestL5_1_EarlyClaim:
  output r content ServiceCreditClaim.CreditClaim

scope TestL5_1_EarlyClaim:
  definition r equals
    output of ServiceCreditClaim.CreditClaim with {
      -- measurement_period_end: |2025-01-31|
      -- claim_made: true
      -- claim_date: |2025-02-03|
      -- claim_accepted_date: |2025-02-10|
      -- further_invoice_expected: true
      -- next_invoice_date: |2025-03-01|
    }
  assertion r.claim_in_time = true
  assertion r.waived = false
```

## L5_1_NoClaimAtAll

L-5.1: "a Service Credit not claimed within that period is waived" catches the
Customer who never claims, not only the one who claims late.

```catala
#[test]
declaration scope TestL5_1_NoClaimAtAll:
  output r content ServiceCreditClaim.CreditClaim

scope TestL5_1_NoClaimAtAll:
  definition r equals
    output of ServiceCreditClaim.CreditClaim with {
      -- measurement_period_end: |2025-01-31|
      -- claim_made: false
      -- claim_date: |2025-02-03|
      -- claim_accepted_date: |2025-02-10|
      -- further_invoice_expected: true
      -- next_invoice_date: |2025-03-01|
    }
  assertion r.claim_in_time = false
  assertion r.waived = true
```

## L5_1_LongMonthDeadline

L-5.1: the deadline is 30 days from the end of the period, not the end of the
following month. April ends on the 30th, so the deadline is 30 May.

```catala
#[test]
declaration scope TestL5_1_LongMonthDeadline:
  output r content ServiceCreditClaim.CreditClaim

scope TestL5_1_LongMonthDeadline:
  definition r equals
    output of ServiceCreditClaim.CreditClaim with {
      -- measurement_period_end: |2025-04-30|
      -- claim_made: true
      -- claim_date: |2025-05-30|
      -- claim_accepted_date: |2025-06-02|
      -- further_invoice_expected: true
      -- next_invoice_date: |2025-07-01|
    }
  assertion r.claim_deadline = |2025-05-30|
  assertion r.claim_in_time = true
  assertion r.waived = false
```

## L5_2_SetOffAgainstNextInvoice

L-5.2 base case: the credit is applied against the next invoice issued after
the claim is accepted.

```catala
#[test]
declaration scope TestL5_2_SetOffAgainstNextInvoice:
  output r content ServiceCreditClaim.CreditClaim

scope TestL5_2_SetOffAgainstNextInvoice:
  definition r equals
    output of ServiceCreditClaim.CreditClaim with {
      -- measurement_period_end: |2025-01-31|
      -- claim_made: true
      -- claim_date: |2025-02-03|
      -- claim_accepted_date: |2025-02-10|
      -- further_invoice_expected: true
      -- next_invoice_date: |2025-03-01|
    }
  assertion r.applied_against_next_invoice = true
  assertion r.paid_to_customer = false
  assertion r.settlement_due_date = |2025-03-01|
```

## L5_2_PaidWhereNoFurtherInvoice

L-5.2 exception: where no further invoice will be issued the credit is paid,
within 30 days of acceptance of the claim.

```catala
#[test]
declaration scope TestL5_2_PaidWhereNoFurtherInvoice:
  output r content ServiceCreditClaim.CreditClaim

scope TestL5_2_PaidWhereNoFurtherInvoice:
  definition r equals
    output of ServiceCreditClaim.CreditClaim with {
      -- measurement_period_end: |2025-01-31|
      -- claim_made: true
      -- claim_date: |2025-02-03|
      -- claim_accepted_date: |2025-02-10|
      -- further_invoice_expected: false
      -- next_invoice_date: |2025-03-01|
    }
  assertion r.applied_against_next_invoice = false
  assertion r.paid_to_customer = true
  assertion r.settlement_due_date = |2025-03-12|
```

## L5_2_SettlementIsIndependentOfWaiver

L-5.1 and L-5.2 answer different questions. A waived credit is still routed by
L-5.2's mechanics, so the two outputs must be read together: `waived` is what
says there is nothing to settle.

```catala
#[test]
declaration scope TestL5_2_SettlementIsIndependentOfWaiver:
  output r content ServiceCreditClaim.CreditClaim

scope TestL5_2_SettlementIsIndependentOfWaiver:
  definition r equals
    output of ServiceCreditClaim.CreditClaim with {
      -- measurement_period_end: |2025-01-31|
      -- claim_made: true
      -- claim_date: |2025-03-03|
      -- claim_accepted_date: |2025-03-10|
      -- further_invoice_expected: false
      -- next_invoice_date: |2025-04-01|
    }
  assertion r.waived = true
  assertion r.applied_against_next_invoice = false
  assertion r.paid_to_customer = true
  assertion r.settlement_due_date = |2025-04-09|
```

## CE0009_TheFactPatternThatCouldNotBeAnswered

CE-0009's own facts. The Measurement Period ended on 31 January 2026, the
claim was made in writing on 5 February 2026, the Supplier accepted it on 10
March 2026 and a further invoice falls due on 1 April 2026. L-5.1 fixes the
deadline at 2 March 2026, so the claim is in time and the waiver does not
operate; L-5.2 applies the credit against the 1 April 2026 invoice. Before the
enum-typed output was removed this scope answered none of it — it raised on
serialisation instead.

```catala
#[test]
declaration scope TestCE0009_TheFactPatternThatCouldNotBeAnswered:
  output r content ServiceCreditClaim.CreditClaim

scope TestCE0009_TheFactPatternThatCouldNotBeAnswered:
  definition r equals
    output of ServiceCreditClaim.CreditClaim with {
      -- measurement_period_end: |2026-01-31|
      -- claim_made: true
      -- claim_date: |2026-02-05|
      -- claim_accepted_date: |2026-03-10|
      -- further_invoice_expected: true
      -- next_invoice_date: |2026-04-01|
    }
  assertion r.claim_deadline = |2026-03-02|
  assertion r.claim_in_time = true
  assertion r.waived = false
  assertion r.applied_against_next_invoice = true
  assertion r.paid_to_customer = false
  assertion r.settlement_due_date = |2026-04-01|
```

## CE0009_TheTwoRoutesAreAlwaysOpposites

L-5.2 admits exactly two routes and no third, so whichever way the exception
hierarchy resolves, exactly one of the two booleans is true. Asserted on both
sides of the only condition that decides it.

```catala
#[test]
declaration scope TestCE0009_TheTwoRoutesAreAlwaysOpposites:
  output with_invoice content ServiceCreditClaim.CreditClaim
  output without_invoice content ServiceCreditClaim.CreditClaim

scope TestCE0009_TheTwoRoutesAreAlwaysOpposites:
  definition with_invoice equals
    output of ServiceCreditClaim.CreditClaim with {
      -- measurement_period_end: |2026-01-31|
      -- claim_made: true
      -- claim_date: |2026-02-05|
      -- claim_accepted_date: |2026-03-10|
      -- further_invoice_expected: true
      -- next_invoice_date: |2026-04-01|
    }
  definition without_invoice equals
    output of ServiceCreditClaim.CreditClaim with {
      -- measurement_period_end: |2026-01-31|
      -- claim_made: true
      -- claim_date: |2026-02-05|
      -- claim_accepted_date: |2026-03-10|
      -- further_invoice_expected: false
      -- next_invoice_date: |2026-04-01|
    }
  assertion with_invoice.applied_against_next_invoice
    = (not with_invoice.paid_to_customer)
  assertion without_invoice.applied_against_next_invoice
    = (not without_invoice.paid_to_customer)
  assertion with_invoice.applied_against_next_invoice = true
  assertion without_invoice.paid_to_customer = true
  assertion without_invoice.settlement_due_date = |2026-04-09|
```
